# FORK: keep our own version of these files on `git merge upstream/master`
# instead of merging upstream's. Requires the "ours" merge driver to be defined
# per-clone: `git config merge.ours.driver true` (done by the session-start hook
# in web containers; run it once manually in local clones). If the driver is not
# defined, git falls back to a normal merge for these files — never worse than
# today. Only list files upstream *also* owns; new fork-only files never conflict.
README.md merge=ours
.github/pull_request_template.md merge=ours
